A void `<?marker>` processing instruction is block-level (like Doctype/HTMLComment):
it always takes its own line inside a children list, regardless of width, and
reindents to its true depth. Both attribute-value forms are covered — a static
literal (verbatim `attr` rendering) and a `{expr}` with a pipeline stage (routed
through attrDoc's ExprAttr case, which renders `name={expr |> stage}` with no
interior spaces, same as any other attribute).

-- input.gsx --
package ui

component Page(id string) {
<div>
<?marker name="results">
					<?marker name={id |> upper}>
</div>
}
-- fmt.golden --
package ui

component Page(id string) {
	<div>
		<?marker name="results">
		<?marker name={id |> upper}>
	</div>
}
